<main><section class="page-head"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Applied ML · Ranking</div><h1>Term Deposit Customer Ranking</h1><p class="section-lead">Turning a low-conversion calling problem into a pre-call ranking problem without letting post-call information leak into the model.</p></div></section><section><div class="container content"><h2>Problem</h2><p>The practical question is not simply whether a customer will subscribe. It is which customers should be contacted first, using only information that would genuinely be known before the call.</p><h2>Approach</h2><ul><li>Separate deployable pre-call features from post-call information.</li><li>Use a transparent baseline alongside a nonlinear challenger.</li><li>Evaluate ranking quality and lift, not accuracy alone.</li><li>Use time-aware validation to test whether performance survives changing conditions.</li></ul><div class="callout">The central modelling decision was to treat prediction timing as part of the problem definition, not as an afterthought.</div><h2>What this case proves</h2><p>I can identify leakage, align modelling choices with a business decision, compare models under realistic validation and translate scores into a usable prioritisation strategy.</p><p><a href="/case-studies">← Back to case studies</a></p></div></section></main>
